# Text formatting

<h2 id="wg-080">Use real headings, lists and tables</h2>

Use the heading, list and table elements, not bold or spaces that only look like them. Start at H2. Do not skip a level.

<%= example('wg-accessible-structure') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| **Bedroom light help** (bold text) | ## Bedroom light help |
| Check the room. • Check the state. (typed bullet characters) | A real list with a lead-in line (see below) |
| A table used to line up a form | A form with labels |

Use a table only for data with at least 2 columns and 3 rows, including the heading row. Put headings in the first row. Do not use a table for layout.

## Lists

Use a bulleted list when the order does not matter. Use numbered steps when it does.

- always use a lead-in line
- start each bullet in lower case, unless it is a name
- do not use more than one sentence in a bullet
- do not put “and” or “or” after the bullets
- do not put a full stop after the last bullet

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Things to check: Plug is in; The hub light is green; and wifi is on. | Check that:<br>- the plug is in<br>- the hub light is green<br>- wifi is on |

## Bold, italics, capitals and quotes

Use bold only for a control the person must select or a label they will see on screen. Do not use italics. Do not write whole sentences in capital letters. Use a blockquote only to quote someone else at length.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| **Important:** do not unplug the hub. | Do not unplug the hub during the update. |
| Press *Save*. | Select **Save**. |
| DO NOT TURN OFF THE HEATING | Do not turn off the heating while the boiler is being serviced. |

<h2 id="wg-081">Do not depend on colour or position</h2>

Say it in words as well as colour, icons and layout.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| A red dot next to the sensor. | Hall sensor: Unavailable (shown with a red dot). |
| See the card on the left. | See the **Heating** card. |

<h2 id="wg-084">Make results reach assistive technology</h2>

When a message appears after an action, put it where a screen reader will announce it. Do not use a toast that disappears before it can be read.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| A coloured banner that fades after 2 seconds. | A status message that stays until the next action: “Request sent. Waiting for the lamp to report.” |
| Help text only shown on hover. | Help text visible under the field. |

## Code and literal values

Use code formatting for an entity ID, key or path that someone must copy. Do not change an underscore, dash or quote mark inside it. See [Technical A to Z](../style-guides/technical-a-to-z.html).
